  <deployScript>// CVE-04 (plan 25-01): create the source and destination tables if they don't
// already exist. mssql-jdbc has no implicit-DDL-on-insert behavior, so both tables are
// created explicitly here, mirroring jdbc-test.xml's sqlite deployScript convention.
//
// Rule 1 fix (discovered during this plan's live verification): the seed row used to be
// INSERTed here too, but the Database Reader's pollOnStart=true poller consumes it within
// the first ~3s of deploy -- well BEFORE run-smoke-test.sh's later
// "Clearing channel statistics" REST call resets the sent/received counters to 0 (that
// call runs once for ALL 32 fixtures, right before the JUnit driver forks) -- so by the
// time MssqlJdbcParamsTest.encryptedReadWrite() actually polls the REST statistics
// endpoint, the real send already happened and was erased by the reset, and no new row
// is ever seeded again. The fix: MssqlJdbcParamsTest seeds its OWN src_records row,
// directly via JDBC, immediately before polling -- mirroring SftpParamsTest.seedAll()'s
// seed-right-before-poll convention (never at deploy time). This deployScript is DDL-only.
var conn = java.sql.DriverManager.getConnection('jdbc:sqlserver://${MSSQL_HOST}:${MSSQL_PORT};databaseName=${MSSQL_DB};encrypt=true;trustServerCertificate=true', '${MSSQL_USER}', '${MSSQL_PASSWORD}');
try {
	var stmt = conn.createStatement();
	stmt.execute("IF OBJECT_ID('src_records', 'U') IS NULL CREATE TABLE src_records (id INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY, patient_name NVARCHAR(255), payload NVARCHAR(MAX), processed BIT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0)");
	stmt.execute("IF OBJECT_ID('dest_records', 'U') IS NULL CREATE TABLE dest_records (id INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY, patient_name NVARCHAR(255), payload NVARCHAR(MAX))");
	stmt.close();
} finally {
	conn.close();
}
return;</deployScript>
